# The badge artwork is copied byte for byte from the entrance site
# (NextOneTwoLabs/nextonetwo-website). core.autocrlf=true on the maintainer
# machine, so without these rules badge.svg (which contains LF line breaks)
# would be committed correctly and then expanded to CRLF on the next checkout,
# breaking byte-identity with the entrance site. Treat all image assets as
# binary: no line-ending conversion.
*.svg -text
*.png -text
# The judged search set's frozen fixtures (#156) keep the line endings they were
# written with. Their checksums are taken over LF text anyway (MF4), so a CRLF
# checkout of any other test file still checks out the same.
tests/search/fixtures/** -text
